src/autoconf of procmail 3.24, regenerated against the snapshot 8b379c4 (27.11.2026):
- no read of the terminal, the removal of _autotst before the test of realloc and
  /usr/local/bin in the default PATH, as before (the patch of the official port for 3.22);
- no benchmark of strstr(): the test program without BENCHSIZE, so that autoconf.h has
  no SLOWstrstr and procmail takes the strstr() of libc. The benchmark times strstr()
  and the substitute of procmail in loops whose results nothing uses, until a second
  has passed; built by GCC 16 at -O3 it did not end (prog-bench run 45938357673:
  "Benchmarking your system's strstr() implementation" until the time out). Its result
  was that of the compiler and of the machine of the build, not of the servers.

